    "section": "HER2-positive EBC",
    "page_start": null,
    "page_end": null,
    "url": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.annonc.2023.11.016",
    "chunk_kind": "recommendation",
    "parent_id": null,
    "text": "For patients with stage I (T1a-b N0) HER2-positive EBC, primary surgery may be carried out [III, B], followed by adjuvant administration of 12 weeks of paclitaxel plus 1 year of trastuzumab if clinical stage is confirmed by pathology [III, B; ESMO-MCBS v1.1 score: A; ESCAT score: I-A].",
    "setting": [
      "early"
    ],
    "subtype": [
      "HR+/HER2+",
      "HR-/HER2+"
    ],
    "line": [
      "adjuvant"
    ],
    "biomarker_tags": [],
    "drugs": [
      "trastuzumab"
    ],
    "evidence": {
      "loe": "III",
      "gor": "B",
      "esmo_mcbs": "A",
      "escat": "I-A"
    },
    "superseded_by": null,
    "copyright_notice": "Copyright © European Society for Medical Oncology. All rights reserved"
  },
  {
    "schema_version": "0.1-draft",
    "chunk_id": "esmo-ebc-2024-02-hrposher2pos-r09",
    "doc_type": "guideline",
    "source": "ESMO-EBC",
    "version": "2024-02",
    "section": "HER2-positive EBC",
    "page_start": null,
    "page_end": null,
    "url": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.annonc.2023.11.016",
    "chunk_kind": "recommendation",
    "parent_id": null,
    "text": "For patients with pathological stage II or III cancer treated with initial surgery, adjuvant ChT combined with 1 year of anti-HER2 therapy should be given [I, A; trastuzumab ESMO-MCBS v1.1 score: A; HP ESMOMCBS v1.1 score: A; ESCAT score: I-A].",
    "setting": [
      "early"
    ],
    "subtype": [
      "HR+/HER2+",
      "HR-/HER2+"
    ],
    "line": [
      "adjuvant"
    ],
    "biomarker_tags": [],
    "drugs": [
      "trastuzumab"
    ],
    "evidence": {
      "loe": "I",
      "gor": "A",
      "esmo_mcbs": "A",
      "escat": "I-A"
    },
    "superseded_by": null,
    "copyright_notice": "Copyright © European Society for Medical Oncology. All rights reserved"
  },
  {
    "schema_version": "0.1-draft",
    "chunk_id": "esmo-ebc-2024-02-hrposher2pos-r10",
    "doc_type": "guideline",
    "source": "ESMO-EBC",
    "version": "2024-02",
    "section": "HER2-positive EBC",
    "page_start": null,
    "page_end": null,
    "url": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.annonc.2023.11.016",
    "chunk_kind": "recommendation",
    "parent_id": null,
    "text": "In patients with node-positive disease, the addition of pertuzumab to trastuzumab should be strongly considered in the adjuvant setting irrespective of HR status [I, A; ESMO-MCBS v1.1 score: A; ESCAT score: I-A].",
    "setting": [
      "early"
    ],
    "subtype": [
      "HR+/HER2+",
      "HR-/HER2+"
    ],
    "line": [
      "adjuvant"
    ],
    "biomarker_tags": [],
    "drugs": [
      "trastuzumab",
      "pertuzumab"
    ],
    "evidence": {
      "loe": "I",
      "gor": "A",
      "esmo_mcbs": "A",
      "escat": "I-A"
    },
    "superseded_by": null,
    "copyright_notice": "Copyright © European Society for Medical Oncology. All rights reserved"
  },
  {
    "schema_version": "0.1-draft",
    "chunk_id": "esmo-ebc-2024-02-hrposher2pos-r11",
    "doc_type": "guideline",
    "source": "ESMO-EBC",
    "version": "2024-02",
    "section": "HER2-positive EBC",
    "page_start": null,
    "page_end": null,
    "url": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.annonc.2023.11.016",
    "chunk_kind": "recommendation",
    "parent_id": null,
    "text": "Patients with high-risk HR-positive tumours may be considered for extended treatment with neratinib (concurrent with ET) for 1 year after completion of 1 year of trastuzumab or trastuzumab-based therapy [I, B; ESMO-MCBS v1.1 score: no evaluable benefit; ESCAT score: I-A].",
    "setting": [
      "early"
    ],
    "subtype": [
      "HR+/HER2+",
      "HR-/HER2+"
    ],
    "line": [
      "adjuvant"
    ],
    "biomarker_tags": [],
    "drugs": [
      "trastuzumab"
    ],
    "evidence": {
      "loe": "I",
      "gor": "B",
      "esmo_mcbs": "A",
      "escat": "I-A"
    },
    "superseded_by": null,
    "copyright_notice": "Copyright © European Society for Medical Oncology. All rights reserved"
  },
  {
    "schema_version": "0.1-draft",
    "chunk_id": "esmo-ebc-2024-02-tnbc-r01",
    "doc_type": "guideline",
    "source": "ESMO-EBC",
    "version": "2024-02",
    "section": "TNBC",
    "page_start": null,
    "page_end": null,
    "url": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.annonc.2023.11.016",
    "chunk_kind": "recommendation",
    "parent_id": null,
    "text": "-  HER2-negative tumours with 1%-9% ER and/or PgR expression (ER-/PgR-low) are a heterogenous group, some of which behave biologically similarly to TNBCs; therapeutic strategies should be adjusted to this specific situation since this might lead to a higher response to ChT and to reduced efficacy of ET compared with classical HR-positive breast cancer [II, B].",
    "setting": [
      "early"
    ],
    "subtype": [
      "TNBC"
    ],
    "line": [
      "adjuvant"
    ],
    "biomarker_tags": [],
    "drugs": [],
    "evidence": {
      "loe": "II",
      "gor": "B",
      "esmo_mcbs": null,
      "escat": null
    },
    "superseded_by": null,
    "copyright_notice": "Copyright © European Society for Medical Oncology. All rights reserved"
  },
  {
    "schema_version": "0.1-draft",
    "chunk_id": "esmo-ebc-2024-02-tnbc-r02",
    "doc_type": "guideline",
    "source": "ESMO-EBC",
    "version": "2024-02",
    "section": "TNBC",
    "page_start": null,
    "page_end": null,
    "url": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.annonc.2023.11.016",
    "chunk_kind": "recommendation",
    "parent_id": null,
    "text": "TNBC tumours should be treated with ChT with or without an ICI (pembrolizumab) [I, A], except for some node-negative special histological subtypes such as secretory or adenoid cystic carcinomas or very low clinical risk (pT1a pN0) tumours [II, B].",
    "setting": [
      "early"
    ],
    "subtype": [
      "TNBC"
    ],
    "line": [
      "adjuvant"
    ],
    "biomarker_tags": [],
    "drugs": [
      "pembrolizumab"
    ],
    "evidence": {
      "loe": "I",
      "gor": "A",
      "esmo_mcbs": null,
      "escat": null
    },
    "superseded_by": null,
    "copyright_notice": "Copyright © European Society for Medical Oncology. All rights reserved"
  },
  {
    "schema_version": "0.1-draft",
    "chunk_id": "esmo-ebc-2024-02-tnbc-r03",
    "doc_type": "guideline",
    "source": "ESMO-EBC",
    "version": "2024-02",
    "section": "TNBC",
    "page_start": null,
    "page_end": null,
    "url": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.annonc.2023.11.016",
    "chunk_kind": "recommendation",
    "parent_id": null,
    "text": "ChT should be administered for 12-24 weeks (4-8 cycles) depending on the stage of the disease, type of selected regimen and regardless of whether an ICI is added [I, A].",
    "setting": [
      "early"
    ],
    "subtype": [
      "TNBC"
    ],
    "line": [
      "adjuvant"
    ],
    "biomarker_tags": [],
    "drugs": [],
    "evidence": {
      "loe": "I",
      "gor": "A",
      "esmo_mcbs": null,
      "escat": null
    },
    "superseded_by": null,
    "copyright_notice": "Copyright © European Society for Medical Oncology. All rights reserved"
  },
  {
    "schema_version": "0.1-draft",
    "chunk_id": "esmo-ebc-2024-02-tnbc-r04",
    "doc_type": "guideline",
    "source": "ESMO-EBC",
    "version": "2024-02",
    "section": "TNBC",
    "page_start": null,
    "page_end": null,
    "url": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.annonc.2023.11.016",
    "chunk_kind": "recommendation",
    "parent_id": null,
    "text": "The use of dose-dense schedules of ChT, with granulocyte colony-stimulating factor support, should be considered given their documented benefit over non-dosedense schedules [I, A].",
    "setting": [
      "early"
    ],
    "subtype": [
      "TNBC"
    ],
    "line": [
      "adjuvant"
    ],
    "biomarker_tags": [],
    "drugs": [],
    "evidence": {
      "loe": "I",
      "gor": "A",
      "esmo_mcbs": null,
      "escat": null
    },
    "superseded_by": null,
    "copyright_notice": "Copyright © European Society for Medical Oncology. All rights reserved"
  },
  {
    "schema_version": "0.1-draft",
    "chunk_id": "esmo-ebc-2024-02-tnbc-r05",
    "doc_type": "guideline",
    "source": "ESMO-EBC",
    "version": "2024-02",
    "section": "TNBC",
    "page_start": null,
    "page_end": null,
    "url": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.annonc.2023.11.016",
    "chunk_kind": "recommendation",
    "parent_id": null,
    "text": "For cT1c-4 N0, or any N-positive TNBC, neoadjuvant treatment is preferred [I, A].",
    "setting": [
      "early"
    ],
    "subtype": [
      "TNBC"
    ],
    "line": [
      "adjuvant"
    ],
    "biomarker_tags": [],
    "drugs": [],
    "evidence": {
      "loe": "I",
      "gor": "A",
      "esmo_mcbs": null,
      "escat": null
    },
    "superseded_by": null,
    "copyright_notice": "Copyright © European Society for Medical Oncology. All rights reserved"
  },
  {
    "schema_version": "0.1-draft",
    "chunk_id": "esmo-ebc-2024-02-tnbc-r06",
    "doc_type": "guideline",
    "source": "ESMO-EBC",
    "version": "2024-02",
    "section": "TNBC",
    "page_start": null,
    "page_end": null,
    "url": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.annonc.2023.11.016",
    "chunk_kind": "recommendation",
    "parent_id": null,
    "text": "cT2-4 N0 or any N-positive (stage II-III) TNBC should be treated with neoadjuvant ChT plus pembrolizumab unless there are risk factors for excessive ICI-associated immune toxicity [I, A; ESMO-MCBS v1.1 score: A].",
    "setting": [
      "early"
    ],
    "subtype": [
      "TNBC"
    ],
    "line": [
      "adjuvant"
    ],
    "biomarker_tags": [],
    "drugs": [
      "pembrolizumab"
    ],
    "evidence": {
      "loe": "I",
      "gor": "A",
      "esmo_mcbs": "A",
      "escat": null
    },
    "superseded_by": null,
    "copyright_notice": "Copyright © European Society for Medical Oncology. All rights reserved"
  },
  {
    "schema_version": "0.1-draft",
    "chunk_id": "esmo-ebc-2024-02-tnbc-r07",
    "doc_type": "guideline",
    "source": "ESMO-EBC",
    "version": "2024-02",
    "section": "TNBC",
    "page_start": null,
    "page_end": null,
    "url": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.annonc.2023.11.016",
    "chunk_kind": "recommendation",
    "parent_id": null,
    "text": "Pembrolizumab should be administered every 3 weeks throughout the neoadjuvant phase [I, A] and for nine 3-week cycles during the adjuvant phase, regardless of pCR status [I, A; ESMO-MCBS v1.1 score: A].",
    "setting": [
      "early"
    ],
    "subtype": [
      "TNBC"
    ],
    "line": [
      "adjuvant"
    ],
    "biomarker_tags": [],
    "drugs": [
      "pembrolizumab"
    ],
    "evidence": {
      "loe": "I",
      "gor": "A",
      "esmo_mcbs": "A",
      "escat": null
    },
    "superseded_by": null,
    "copyright_notice": "Copyright © European Society for Medical Oncology. All rights reserved"
  },
  {
    "schema_version": "0.1-draft",
    "chunk_id": "esmo-ebc-2024-02-tnbc-r08",
    "doc_type": "guideline",
    "source": "ESMO-EBC",
    "version": "2024-02",
    "section": "TNBC",
    "page_start": null,
    "page_end": null,
    "url": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.annonc.2023.11.016",
    "chunk_kind": "recommendation",
    "parent_id": null,
    "text": "Patients receiving pembrolizumab should be monitored very closely for the risk of immune-related adverse events throughout treatment and following the ESMO CPG for the management of toxicities from immunotherapy [V, A]. 107",
    "setting": [
      "early"
    ],
    "subtype": [
      "TNBC"
    ],
    "line": [
      "adjuvant"
    ],
    "biomarker_tags": [],
    "drugs": [
      "pembrolizumab"
    ],
    "evidence": {
      "loe": "V",
      "gor": "A",
      "esmo_mcbs": null,
      "escat": null
    },
    "superseded_by": null,
    "copyright_notice": "Copyright © European Society for Medical Oncology. All rights reserved"
  },
  {
    "schema_version": "0.1-draft",
    "chunk_id": "esmo-ebc-2024-02-tnbc-r09",
    "doc_type": "guideline",
    "source": "ESMO-EBC",
    "version": "2024-02",
    "section": "TNBC",
    "page_start": null,
    "page_end": null,
    "url": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.annonc.2023.11.016",
    "chunk_kind": "recommendation",
    "parent_id": null,
    "text": "An ICI should not be given solely in the adjuvant setting without prior neoadjuvant ICI treatment [V, D].",
